TITLE:: SDGReturn
summary:: a return track as in Ableton: a send knob on every orbit, inserts, an effect, a fader, and sends to other returns for feedback
categories:: Libraries>SuperDirtGUI
related:: Classes/SuperDirtGUI, Classes/SDGTrack, Classes/SDGInsert, Classes/SDGWindow, Classes/SDGSession

DESCRIPTION::
A return is one track that any orbit can send to, so one reverb serves them all.
The link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI:: makes it, and the window shows it as a strip
after the orbits.

code::
a = ~sdg.addReturn;                       // return A
~sdg.setReturnEffect(a, \dirt_reverb);    // or none, and only inserts
~sdg.setSend(0, a, 0.5);                  // orbit 0 into it, -6 dB
a.level = 0.7;                            // what comes back
a.preFader = true;                        // sends into it ignore the source's fader
~sdg.addTrackInsert(a, \post, \eq);       // inserts, as on an orbit's track

b = ~sdg.addReturn;                       // return B
~sdg.returnFeedback = true;               // returns may send to returns
~sdg.setReturnSend(a, b, 0.4);            // A into B
~sdg.setReturnSend(b, a, 0.4);            // and back: a loop
::

subsection:: The signal

An orbit's send sits in the orbit's chain, right before its fader: it hears the
effects and inserts, and it comes back with the orbit from every rebuild. The
return runs in a group of its own after SuperDirt's, so everything the orbits
sent this block is there to read.

code::
// orbit:  ... inserts, sends, fader, rms, monitor
// heads:  each return's sends in, and last block's feedback
// return: pre inserts, effect, mix, post inserts, sends to returns, out
::

The effect comes out fully wet. With no effect, or with it off, the line passes
as it came. Effects start at values that are heard (link::#*wetDefaults::),
because most are silent at their SynthDef's defaults. All buses and the output
are code::numChannels:: wide.

subsection:: Rules for sends

Taken from Ableton:

list::
## link::#-preFader:: says whether what goes into this return is taken before or after the source's fader. It is post fader by default.
## A muted source sends nothing, pre fader or not.
## A soloed orbit keeps its returns audible, and the other orbits' sends stop.
## A soloed return stops the orbits' direct sound and every other return, while what is sent to it goes on.
::

subsection:: Feedback

Sends between returns are only heard while link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-returnFeedback:: is
on, off by default. A knob keeps its level while it is off, so a loop can be set up
first. A return can also send to itself.

Each send between returns arrives exactly one block later (64 samples, 1.3 ms at
48 kHz), whatever the order of the returns and the shape of the loop. Each return
reads that feedback from a bus of its own, before any return of this block has
written. On a bus shared with the orbits' sends, the first write of the block would wipe it.

The feedback input saturates softly from +6 dB, and bad values become silence, so a
loop with gain above 1 screams at a bounded level instead of running away. It can still
be loud: keep the limiter on.

subsection:: Who owns what

The link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI:: makes and frees returns. A return never sleeps: no
event reaches it, so a tick once a second resumes its effect and inserts, and a tail
never gets cut. After a cmd-period everything comes back with its levels, a VST plugin
with the state it last read back. link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-reload:: keeps returns and
starts their effects again on the new SynthDefs. A link::Classes/SDGSession:: saves them.
A return's effect parameters are not Tidal's: they live in its own
link::#-defaultParentEvent::.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Made by link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-addReturn::, not by hand.
ARGUMENT:: sdg
the link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI::.
ARGUMENT:: letter
its letter, a Symbol.

METHOD:: isReturnName
Whether a name is that of a return's plumbing.
ARGUMENT:: name
a Symbol or String.
RETURNS:: a link::Classes/Boolean::.

METHOD:: makeDefs
Add the SynthDefs of a return.
ARGUMENT:: numChannels
the channel count.

METHOD:: wetDefaults
What an effect starts at on a return: known ones for stock delay and reverb, and a
content effect's parameter named after it at 1.
ARGUMENT:: name
the effect's name.
ARGUMENT:: paramNames
its parameters.
RETURNS:: an link::Classes/Event::.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: letter
RETURNS:: its letter, a link::Classes/Symbol::.

METHOD:: shortName
RETURNS:: what a person calls it: "return A".

METHOD:: fx
RETURNS:: its link::Classes/GlobalDirtEffect::, nil without one. Use link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-setReturnEffect:: to change it.

METHOD:: name
RETURNS:: its effect's name, nil without one.

METHOD:: effectOn
Whether the effect runs. Off, the line passes as if it were not there.
ARGUMENT:: bool
true or false.

METHOD:: level
The fader, an amplitude from 0 to 4.
ARGUMENT:: amp
the amplitude.

METHOD:: muted
RETURNS:: whether it is muted. Set it with link::#-mute::.

METHOD:: mute
Mute it, and what it sends to other returns.
ARGUMENT:: bool
true or false.

METHOD:: soloed
RETURNS:: whether it is soloed. Set it with link::#-solo::.

METHOD:: solo
Solo it. See link::#Rules for sends::.
ARGUMENT:: bool
true or false.

METHOD:: preFader
Whether what is sent into this return is taken before the source's fader.
ARGUMENT:: bool
true or false.

METHOD:: limitertype
The output's guard: 0 nothing, 1 a limiter, 2 a soft clip.
ARGUMENT:: value
the number.

METHOD:: outBus
The bus it writes to; at first orbit 0's.
ARGUMENT:: index
a bus number, or a link::Classes/Bus::.

METHOD:: orbitLevel
ARGUMENT:: orbitIndex
the orbit's number.
RETURNS:: the level of that orbit's send, 0 to 1.

METHOD:: returnLevel
ARGUMENT:: target
another SDGReturn, or this one.
RETURNS:: the level of the send to it, 0 to 1.

METHOD:: targets
RETURNS:: the returns it can send to: all of them, itself too.

METHOD:: pre
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/SDGInsert::s before the effect, in signal order.

METHOD:: post
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/SDGInsert::s after the effect, in signal order.

METHOD:: inserts
RETURNS:: both lists as one.

METHOD:: lineBus
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/Bus:: its inserts and effect work on.

METHOD:: tapBus
RETURNS:: the link::Classes/Bus:: holding what it plays, after its fader: what the recorder reads.

METHOD:: defaultParentEvent
RETURNS:: its effect's parameters, the values the window's knobs set.

METHOD:: nodes
RETURNS:: its chain's synths in signal order, without the head.

METHOD:: metering
Whether it sends its levels as code::'/sdgtrack'::, 20 a second. The window turns this on.
ARGUMENT:: bool
true or false.
